From: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: fetch hardware counters before removing a flow

The counters of hardware offloaded flows are added to conntrack by the
stats work, which nf_flow_offload_stats() queues only after a tenth of
the flow timeout has passed since the last update, i.e. about every 3 s
with the default nf_flowtable_tcp_timeout of 30 s. When a flow is torn
down, e.g. on a TCP FIN or RST, flow_offload_work_del() removes the
hardware entries without fetching their counters, so the traffic since
the last poll never reaches conntrack.

At gigabit speeds that is easily a hundred megabytes per connection: a
300 MiB HTTPS download that closes its connection right away was
accounted at 69-84% by nlbwmon on a MT7622, and at 105% (payload plus
headers) when the connection stayed open for a few seconds first.

Fetch the counters once more in the delete work before removing the
hardware entries. The flow and its conntrack entry are still referenced
there: NF_FLOW_HW_DEAD is only set after the worker is done.

Signed-off-by: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
@@ -987,14 +987,6 @@
 	nf_flow_offload_destroy(flow_rule);
 }
 
-static void flow_offload_work_del(struct flow_offload_work *offload)
-{
-	clear_bit(IPS_HW_OFFLOAD_BIT, &offload->flow->ct->status);
-	flow_offload_tuple_del(offload, FLOW_OFFLOAD_DIR_ORIGINAL);
-	if (test_bit(NF_FLOW_HW_BIDIRECTIONAL, &offload->flow->flags))
-		flow_offload_tuple_del(offload, FLOW_OFFLOAD_DIR_REPLY);
-}
-
 static void flow_offload_tuple_stats(struct flow_offload_work *offload,
 				     enum flow_offload_tuple_dir dir,
 				     struct flow_stats *stats)
@@ -1031,6 +1023,22 @@
 	}
 }
 
+static void flow_offload_work_del(struct flow_offload_work *offload)
+{
+	/*
+	 * Stats are only polled every few seconds: fetch the counters of the
+	 * hardware entries one last time before they are removed, so that the
+	 * traffic since the last poll is not lost for conntrack accounting.
+	 */
+	if (offload->flowtable->flags & NF_FLOWTABLE_COUNTER)
+		flow_offload_work_stats(offload);
+
+	clear_bit(IPS_HW_OFFLOAD_BIT, &offload->flow->ct->status);
+	flow_offload_tuple_del(offload, FLOW_OFFLOAD_DIR_ORIGINAL);
+	if (test_bit(NF_FLOW_HW_BIDIRECTIONAL, &offload->flow->flags))
+		flow_offload_tuple_del(offload, FLOW_OFFLOAD_DIR_REPLY);
+}
+
 static void flow_offload_work_handler(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	struct flow_offload_work *offload;
